--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -2,6 +2,22 @@
 
 This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
 
+## View caching
+
+The shared layout retains up to five page-content views in memory, including the
+active view. Returning to a cached URL reuses its DOM and mounted islands. Inactive
+views use `content-visibility: hidden`, `inert`, and `aria-hidden`; browsers without
+content visibility fall back to `display: none`. The least recently used view is
+removed when the cache fills.
+
+The cache integrates with [Astro's swap lifecycle](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/view-transitions/#astrobefore-swap),
+retaining the styles needed by cached views while Astro manages history, scroll,
+metadata, and scripts. Navigation still fetches the destination document; this
+cache saves DOM reconstruction and rendering work, not network requests. Query
+strings identify separate views, while fragments share a view. Same-URL refreshes
+replace that view, and router-handled form submissions invalidate the cache.
+Reloading the document clears all cached views.
+
 
 ```sh
 pnpm install && pnpm run start
